From 24f32107652f04333651596f3945a65768ca9699 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: atomozero <bernardi.andrea@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 07:20:23 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 28/63] kernel/arm: caches, page tables and the PL310 outer
 cache

- write page table updates back to memory; invalidate the TLBs and
  instruction caches of all CPUs; make newly executable pages coherent
  with the instruction cache
- map write combining memory as normal non-cacheable, and flush the data
  cache when memory becomes non-cacheable
- write-allocate caching
- report the right modified flag when unmapping pages, keep a page
  modified when its mapping becomes read-only, never take physical
  address 0 for an unmapped page
- map the kept boot loader ranges per physically contiguous run, and do
  not let the boot range unmapping wrap around at the top of the address
  space
- the PL310 outer cache, left off unless asked for

Signed-off-by: atomozero <bernardi.andrea@gmail.com>
